# Design Tokens

Values live in Foundations (`packages/ui/src/foundations/`). This rule states usage only. Rationale: `docs/DESIGN.md`.

Primitives and composition tiers (atoms → templates) must pass `pnpm check:tokens` (CI gate). Vendor output under `src/components/ui` is not hand-edited — `pnpm check:tokens:vendor` is informational only.

## Dimensions

- Spacing tokens are for rhythm only (padding, gaps, margins) — never for sizing components.
- Do not invent height/width tokens: those sizes are usually content-, padding-, and line-height-driven, and Figma does not define them.
- Border-radius uses Foundations radius tokens — never raw `rounded-[…px|rem]`.

## Icons

- Size always from `--icon-*`, including when sizing via icon-context selectors (`[&>svg]:…`, `[&_svg]:…`, `svg:…`). Never hardcoded px on icons.
- Glyphs: Lucide for system UI, Solar Bold Duotone for illustrative accents. Never mix sets in one interface.

## Colors

- Semantic color classes only. Never hex literals.

## Motion

- No duration/easing tokens exist yet. Do not invent them.
- On second use of the same motion value, promote it to Foundations.
